                <pb facs="0565" n="485" sameAs="frus:frus1936v01/pg485"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.C1112/90a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Consul at
                        Geneva</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grilbert</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-12-31T16:00:00-05:00">December 31,
                            1936—4 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>163. Please suggest to Stoppani that he may wish to consider appointment to
                    Economic Committee of Mr. Henry F. Grady, Dean of the College of Commerce and
                    Professor of International Trade, University of California, Berkeley,
                    California. In case he is appointed and the Council proceeds with organization
                    of Raw Materials Committee, Council might provide that the American Member of
                    the Economic Committee be a member of the Raw Materials Committee. Grady is
                    regarded as exceptionally qualified both by experience and continuing
                    relationships to explain American policies and is prepared to accept these
                    appointments.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moore</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
